{
  "dom_id": "step-q134122",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/f2f569fe07310e8bd068cda0152b296d7b1189efec03720a0d3a043a7ab52d21.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the relationship between the age of some people and the average number of cups of coffee they consume daily. \nWhich of the following is the best approximation of the correlation coefficient?",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the linear correlation coefficient $\\rho $ satisfies the inequality\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\rho \\le 1,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\rho =1$ indicates a perfect positive correlation, and $\\rho =-1$ indicates a perfect negative correlation.\n\nFrom the plot, it seems that the data points are scattered randomly. Therefore, there is no linear correlation.\n\nTherefore, the best approximation of the correlation coefficient must be $\\rho ≈0.$",
